 is documented as being the official standard for that language.

  The "System Libraries" of an executable work means the works that
 are included in the normal form of packaging a Major Component, but
 are not part of the work, and to run it with that work, are
 components of the operating system or generally distributed among
 the developers of a Major Component (e.g., the C Standard Library,
 the C++ Standard Library, and system libraries needed for the
 running of an executable work).  "Major Components" are the works
 that are the primary components of an operating system, or
 generally included in the normal distribution of a major
 component, or that are generally distributed as separate files
 that are arranged to be used with a Major Component.

  The "Corresponding Source" for a work in object code form means all
